    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Preventing kitchen accidents requires understanding the specific hazards of <span class=\"learn-keyword\">cuts</span>, <span class=\"learn-keyword\">suffocation</span>, and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">accidental poisoning</span> and applying targeted preventive measures. Prevention is always better than treatment — a safe kitchen environment protects all members of the household.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Measures to Prevent Cuts</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Use sharp knives (dull knives require more force — slipping and cutting accidents are more common)</li>\n  <li>Always cut away from the body, on a stable chopping board</li>\n  <li>Keep fingers curled ('bear claw' grip) when guiding food for cutting</li>\n  <li>Never leave knives in a sink of water (invisible and dangerous)</li>\n  <li>Store knives safely in a knife block, on a magnetic strip, or with blade guards</li>\n  <li>Handle broken glass carefully — sweep, never pick up with bare hands</li>\n  <li>Open tin cans away from the body; file sharp edges of opened tins</li>\n  <li>Keep kitchen areas well-lit to see sharp objects clearly</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Measures to Prevent Suffocation</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Suffocation in the kitchen can occur from gas leaks, carbon monoxide, or choking:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Ensure adequate ventilation when cooking (open windows, use extractor fan)</li>\n  <li>Check gas connections and hoses regularly for leaks (soapy water test: bubbles indicate leaks)</li>\n  <li>Install a carbon monoxide alarm if using gas or solid fuel appliances</li>\n  <li>Do not use charcoal grills or kerosene stoves in enclosed spaces</li>\n  <li>Supervise young children during meals (choking hazard — small, firm foods)</li>\n  <li>Cut food into appropriate sizes for young children</li>\n  <li>Know the Heimlich manoeuvre for choking emergencies</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Measures to Prevent Accidental Poisoning</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Store all cleaning products and chemicals in original, clearly labelled containers</li>\n  <li>Keep cleaning products in locked cupboards away from children's reach</li>\n  <li>Never store chemicals in food containers (confusion risk)</li>\n  <li>Keep medicines in separate, clearly labelled containers with childproof caps</li>\n  <li>Properly dispose of expired medications — do not keep in kitchen</li>\n  <li>Be aware of toxic plants in home gardens that children might access</li>\n  <li>Ensure all food is properly stored to prevent mould and spoilage toxins (aflatoxins)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> CUTS: sharp knives safer than dull (less force needed); bear claw grip; knives out of sink; store safely. SUFFOCATION: ventilation, CO alarm, gas check, no charcoal in enclosed spaces. POISONING: original labelled containers, childproof storage, never in food containers. Aflatoxins from mouldy stored food (maize, groundnuts) are a poisoning risk.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Prevent cuts: sharp knives, cut away from body, bear claw, safe storage, no knives in sink, handle glass carefully. Prevent suffocation: ventilation, gas checks, CO alarm, no charcoal indoors, supervise children eating. Prevent poisoning: labelled containers, locked storage, never in food containers, dispose of expired chemicals, store food properly to prevent mould toxins.\n</div>\n  ",
